  ('zcrm_1579374000168866044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117873002', 'Marc Marlowe', NULL, '7/28/25
Received a call from a representative at (951) 319-4891 named Bon Lewis, calling on behalf of Patricia Marlowe to verify eligibility. Unfortunately, the representative had a thick accent, and it was difficult to understand him clearly.

He stated that he was calling to confirm the member''s deductible and eligibility. I asked what type of consultation the member was scheduled for, but he did not answer and was acting strangely. He then requested the payer ID and group number.

I explained that we do not function like traditional health insurance and asked for the procedure details. He eventually stated it was for pathology. I informed him that the patient would be presenting as self-pay and that any billing questions would need to go through us directly. Despite this, he continued to insist on getting a payer ID.

I reiterated that we do not issue a payer ID because patients present as self-pay for non-preventative services. The representative became upset and stated that, as the eligibility department, I should have this information. I repeated that the insurance card only covers preventative services and would not apply to the upcoming appointment. At that point, the representative ended the call abruptly. AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-07-28 11:11:57', '2025-07-28 11:11:57'),
