  ('zcrm_1579374000168270289', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000159732002', 'Chad Moore', NULL, 'Member submitted Change Form to remove spouse &amp; dependents that we spoke about 2 days ago per note below.  Change will be effective 8/1/25.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-07-17 11:41:47', '2025-07-17 11:41:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000168298217', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000062250051', 'Cody Bennett', NULL, '7-17-25 Dear CODY JAMES BENNETT,
 
Your insurance premium is past due. Please make a payment to keep your plan active.
 
Your Medical payment of $163.64 was not received and is now past due. Please pay the full past due amount now. If we don’t receive your payment, your policy will be terminated and you’ll lose your coverage. You should know that depending on when we receive your payment this past due balance may still be listed in your next month’s bill.
 
Due to your past due status, you will not receive benefits for your prescription costs. Once the full balance of your account has been paid and posted, your pharmacy benefits will be restored.
 
Please disregard this notice if you have already paid your full balance.
 
Your next steps:
•  Log into http://www.cigna.com to pay online, using one of our approved payment methods, or
•  Pay with your bank account information by calling 1-877-900-1237
 
Sign up for Electronic Funds Transfer (EFT) and never miss a payment again. Each month, we will automatically charge your bank account the amount of your premium. You won’t need to mail us anything and your payments will always be on time. To sign up for EFT, please call us at 1-877-900-1237. It will take one to two months to start EFT. Continue to send us your payments by mail until we have it set up.
 
If you have any questions, please call us at: 1-877-900-1237 during normal business hours.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-17 11:40:07', '2025-07-17 11:40:07'),
