  ('zcrm_1579374000168246177', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000168251003', 'Edward Moore', NULL, 'Member &amp; Sp $5000 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-07-16 13:19:57', '2025-07-16 13:19:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000168270044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000076954787', 'Christopher Megroz', NULL, '7-16-25 Gordy was shocked by the price increase since he''s turning 50. It''s now $1018 at $1000. But, he looked into other options via Tess'' new employer and that was way more expensive and worse benefits. They were struggling to get Zion to share in Tess'' accident to her broken tooth but they finally got it sorted out and they are paying their $1000 IUA. Gordy has a thumb issue that he opened the Need for about 1+ ago. It''s likely more than 1 year. He paid $300 towards it and knows if it''s over a year, he''ll have to pay the full $1000 towards the need. He thinks he will need surgery on it soon. It''s starting to cause problems. Sophie needs the ACA compliant annual wellness screenings. So, they will remain on course for now until they are past all of their Needs and then we could possibly look to make a switch. He realizes it''s still way more affordable than the alternatives at this point.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-07-16 13:14:12', '2025-07-16 13:14:12'),
