  ('zcrm_1579374000168178096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155179018', 'Annie Fisher', NULL, '7/15/25: Annie (natalie?) emailed in the following questions: 
Hi, There are so many different providers(?) for different services that keep changing. Zion Healthshare? ARM Alternative Risk Management etc. It''s like a maze trying to understand all the ins and outs. Is there a master list?
Also,  What are the instructions for going to an emergency room? Show them my health card? And say what?

Response:
Yes, it can seem overwhelming at first. Essentially, there are no network provider restrictions for any need that is diagnostic. If you are sick, have an incident (ER), or trying to diagnose an issue, you would present as self-pay. Any eligible expenses that go over your IUA are submitted to and shared through Zion. 

If you go to the ER, tell them you are a self-pay patient and ask for a cash discount. 

Your plan also has a MEC – (minimum essential coverage) that pays for the preventive services outlined in the ACA Guidelines on healthcare.gov. 
Altrisk Management (ARM) is your MEC provider and pays 100% of any of these services as long as you go to a provider within the PHCS network – which you can access here. 

This website is the master list for all providers within the PHCS network.

I hope this answers your questions. Feel free to call us at any time. We’re happy to walk you through using the different pieces of your plan. It’s why we’re here! 
AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-07-15 08:15:20', '2025-07-15 08:15:20'),
