  ('zcrm_1579374000167761028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000158944002', 'Sebastian Aviles', NULL, '7/7/25
Sebastian Calle called today reporting ongoing symptoms including cold sores in his mouth, fever, and chills. He previously had a virtual consultation with a physician via CirrusMD on July 3, during which he was prescribed antibiotics. However, he reports no improvement in his condition and is now seeking an in-person evaluation.

I explained that an in-person visit would be out-of-pocket until he meets his IUA (Initial Unshareable Amount) and that Zion will only share in eligible expenses after that amount is met.

I advised Sebastian to consider visiting urgent care or a primary care provider (PCP) who can evaluate his condition and refer him to a specialist if needed. He expressed confusion regarding the differences between specialty care, preventative care, and primary care. I provided a brief explanation of each, including the appropriate uses of urgent care versus emergency room visits.

Despite my recommendation to seek urgent care for faster evaluation, Sebastian insisted on seeing a dermatologist, as he believes that is the type of specialist he needs. AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-07-07 09:28:20', '2025-07-07 10:16:37'),
