  ('zcrm_1579374000167704011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021919047', 'Tatiana Moroz', NULL, '7/3/25
Tatiana called to inquire about opening a sharing request related to a recent miscarriage. She explained that it was an anembryonic pregnancy (empty gestational sac). I informed her that Sedera may not share in this situation, as it may be viewed similarly to an elective abortion, despite there being no embryo. I emphasized the complexity of the issue due to Sedera’s status as a medical cost-sharing community rather than traditional insurance, and that this situation falls into a gray area.

Tatiana shared that she has **already expelled everything** and now needs an **ultrasound** to confirm that everything has passed. She also wants to see a **specialist** to understand why she was unable to carry the pregnancy to term.

I explained that:
Fertility-related issues are not eligible for sharing.
The MEC (Minimum Essential Coverage) plan only covers preventive services.

She was understandably frustrated by this information.

To support her, I:
Offered assistance in researching more affordable ultrasound providers.
Offered help in finding  cost-effective specialists for follow-up care.

Tatiana also mentioned that she read online about the possibility of having certain **antibodies** that could have impacted her pregnancy and is interested in a **shot to suppress them** to support future pregnancies. I reiterated my willingness to help locate providers who could explore and discuss these concerns with her.
AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-07-03 10:49:56', '2025-07-03 10:49:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000167716001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032454006', 'Georgannna Garrison', NULL, '07/03/20025
