  ('zcrm_1579374000167261166', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000164112010', 'Megan Berry', NULL, '6-25-25 After a long conversation with Meg she decided it''s better to remain with Care+ long term for the monthly savings vs Premium Care. She due Nov. 25th . So, it could mean only 4 months of payments that would count towards maternity, then they have to meet the $2500 IUA and then the final costs may be shared which be max $1600 since she didn''t want to lower the IUA. Plus she already has paid $700 towards the midwife and has an ultrasound at the end of July.  She might pre-pay the rest of the maternity. So, it was starting to get really complicated and possibly not worth the change.  They have the money saved. They will likely have to move in the midst while pregnant, planning a wedding and taking care of two kids already. They are doing well though.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-06-25 20:23:37', '2025-06-25 20:23:37'),
