  ('zcrm_1579374000166983016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109649002', 'Sean Clouse', NULL, '6/20/25: Called to FU with Marcianna regarding her rx issue and ended up speaking to Sean. We discussed why the rx were not ringing up for $0 last time they went to pharmacy and the kinks that rx valet was having in the beginning. Let him know to please call us if that happens again and explained that if it says zero, he should be able to get first 30 at pharmacy and then continue meds through mail order for 0. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-06-20 07:31:01', '2025-06-20 07:31:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166984012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000166955002', 'Joseph Rakoski', NULL, 'Member &amp; Fam $2500 IUA Secure', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-06-20 07:29:36', '2025-06-20 07:29:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166984004', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000166954001', 'Abra Katterhenry', NULL, 'Member Only $1000 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-06-20 07:24:58', '2025-06-20 07:24:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166983001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130562001', 'Philip Ender', NULL, '6/20/25: Esther emailed in asking if she needs to see a PCP first to see a dermatologist and if the derm needs to be in-network. I replied:
•	For an annual skin cancer check, that would need to be done during an annual visit with a PCP to be paid for using your preventive service benefits.
•	Many skin conditions can be treated using telehealth such as rashes or acne. 
•	For more serious issues that require an in-person visit, there are no network restrictions, and you would be presenting as self-pay. Any eligible expenses that exceed your IUA can be submitted for sharing.
AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-06-20 07:15:04', '2025-06-20 07:15:04'),
