  ('zcrm_1579374000166870006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000168202017', 'Sean Coyne', NULL, '6-18-25 Janet Coyne called to get insurance for her son who is turning 26 in Aug. DOB 8/20/1999, 80027. He''s living at home with parents and not working. He may be a little autistic but he''s never been tested. He''s never worked, so he doesn''t file taxes. Therefore, he won''t be able to qualify for Medicaid without filing taxes. Janet prefers to pay full price. She created the account and made it through to choosing a plan. She put Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $0 for $344 or $341.22. We will meet again July 15th for her to complete the process for an Aug. 1st start date. He will need to show proof of losing coverage under his parents due to his age. He also take 3 meds for his anxiety. Buproprion HCL ER 300mg, alprazolam and sertraline 100 mg and half pill for 150 mg. She''s happy with the plan I recommended.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-06-18 16:57:21', '2025-06-18 16:57:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166847029', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000132469002', 'Tymon Skidmore', NULL, '6/18/25: Alana called wanting to know more about their rx benefits. I explained the concierge service and emailed her the quote form. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-06-18 16:47:24', '2025-06-18 16:47:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166847022', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013233260', 'Brandy Echery', NULL, '6/18/25: Ellis called wondering if his plan pays for a cologuard. I let him know that yes it does since it''s a colon cancer screening - however it can become sticky bc if the cologuard comes back positive then a future colonoscopy could be considered diagnostic which wouldn''t be paid for at 100% - it would be a sharing request. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-06-18 16:17:11', '2025-06-18 16:17:11'),
