  ('zcrm_1579374000166804061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000057645404', 'James (JP) Boylan', NULL, '6/18/25

Julie called regarding a charge from her 4/16/25 appointment. She stated that only \$29 was covered by insurance, but her plan should cover preventive services at 100%. I informed her that I did not see a claim submitted as preventive for that date of service and advised her to contact the provider to have the claim resubmitted. I mentioned it may have been mistakenly sent to another plan (possibly Planstin).

A few minutes later, a representative from Boulder Medical Center called to confirm they would be resubmitting the claim. Upon further review, it appears the visit was coded as an office visit rather than a preventive service.

I explained to the rep that the member, Juliane, believed the appointment was preventive. I also clarified that her plan only covers ACA-mandated preventive services at 100%. The rep informed me that Juliane was originally scheduled for a wellness check, but that appointment was canceled, and this visit was actually scheduled as a new patient appointment instead.

