  ('zcrm_1579374000166744502', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000168462023', 'David Tracht', NULL, '6-17-25 David 51 and Ann 51 with 2 kids 20 son and 18 daughter. David is leaving his job soon to become self-employed. Ann is already self-employed. Cobra will be about $3500 EF! Ann likes to do her annual wellness screenings, including pap, mammo, colonoscopy, PCP visit and skin check. Their son had nasal surgery for general congestion and that didn''t solve the problem. Now they are focusing on allergies and he''s taking a med for that. They know this is pre-x. David has diverticulitis about 3 years ago in Dec. 2022 and then March of 2023 he had part of an intestine removed, so he will never have that problem again. No others meds, no tobacco for anyone. They live in Atlanta GA. They want to price out ACA as well. I talked with Diane Border and she''s happy to help them with ACA. Their household income is $250K-$300K, so they won''t qualify for a subsidy. Ann already did her colonoscopy within the past year or so. No need for that. They were referred to me by Dan and Florie Glusman. They watched the video which was super hlepful to simplify the conversation. They are most interested in Premium HSA $1000/$988 or $1500/$895.  Also, Ann wants to keep Dr. Scott Ramshur in Piedmont Physicians of Sandy Springs. He''s not showing up in the Multiplan search and the provider''s site doesn''t show the insurance companies. So, I asked them to call the drs. office to verify if they accept the PHCS/MultiPlan network. They will do so. Ann takes a HRT 50 mcg/ 140 mcg and gets as many patches as possible. I found it for a good price on Pharmacy Checker - 

