  ('zcrm_1579374000166695006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000164309002', 'Tammy Morrison', NULL, 'Member submitted a change form with no information as to what she wanted changed.  I left her a VM and she called in after hours and told me that she wanted to yet again push her start date to 8/1/25.  I will do this one last time and let member know that if she doesn''t want to start on 8/1 she will have to re-enroll.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-06-16 07:00:11', '2025-06-16 07:00:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166695001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120264002', 'Cheryl Powell', NULL, 'Member called in to let me know that she will need to cancel due to a lack of funds.  I will send her out the link.  She was originally a member of Jeffrey''s', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-06-16 06:53:05', '2025-06-16 06:53:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166637149', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061924134', 'Kristen Lassalette', NULL, '6-13-25 From Ashlee - Hi Wendy, 

Here’s what I found out.

We contacted her provider and spoke with a Rachell from their office and informed her that we received the corrected claims, but we did not receive the required proof of timely filing. She confirmed that they’re unable to provide that documentation but mentioned they would reach out to the member directly to help resolve the balance. She also stated they would contact us if they had any further questions.

Given this response and the lack of follow-up from the provider, we assumed they were working with the member directly to resolve the matter.

Unfortunately, since they’re unwilling to provide the necessary documentation for us to process payment—and have indicated they’ll handle it with the member—there’s little more we can do at this point. While we’re always happy to explain our requirements and processes to providers, we ultimately can’t control whether they choose to comply.

Ashlee Williams

This was my response:

Hi Ashlee,

This has been a bit of a disaster from start to finish. AVH can''t supply you with timely filing because they were told numerous times by Planstin Reps that they must submit the bill to the member. They tried to submit the bill to Kirsten and then Kristen was told by the MPB  Concierge and I that AVH must file the claim directly with Planstin.  Planstin has always required MPB members to ask the provider to bill directly to Planstin and NOT to bill the member. 

After going in circles for months nothing was resolved. Now it''s past the 6 month deadline partially due to Planstin''s wrong information given to Kristen on numerous occasions. I believe you have record of all of those calls to show proof.  If that''s not sufficient, what do you want them to provide, in light of false communications made by Planstin to Kristen and AVH numerous times? 

Hopefully you can take care of this once and for all. Thanks a ton Ashlee!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-06-13 16:40:54', '2025-06-13 16:40:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000166683001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000065104128', 'Lindsay Tollefson', NULL, '06.13.25:  Responded to Lindsay''s email of 6.5.25 thanking Patti and me for all our help &amp; info. She wrote she has applied for her Medicare card, is looking at different plans and will consider maintaining the MPB Healthcare Essentials plan.Told her to contact me w/any questions or if she decides to enroll in the MPB Essentials plan. JSP', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2025-06-13 15:15:45', '2025-06-13 15:15:45'),
