  ('zcrm_1579374000166374032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077566026', 'MaiLan Boris', NULL, 'Contacted Milan to inform her that when polyps are removed during a screening colonoscopy, the procedure is reclassified as diagnostic. As a result, MEC will not cover the cost.
Milan stated that a representative from ARM told her that if the original coding was preventive, it could be waived. I explained that at the time of her colonoscopy, she was covered under Planstin, which has strict policies regarding diagnostic coding.
She expressed frustration and mentioned that ARM had sent her the rejection notice. I clarified that the notice came from ARM because they are not responsible for covering that specific bill, and that it should be submitted to Planstin. I advised her to have her provider send the bill to Planstin for review.
Milan also mentioned that another representative had advised her to use her ARM card, which I explained was not accurate. She appeared to believe I was arguing with her and ended the call. Ac', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-06-09 10:11:36', '2025-06-09 10:11:36'),
