  ('zcrm_1579374000166041001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000161000002', 'James Vega', NULL, '6/3/25: James emailed in the following: 
Hello,  Trying to set up an appt for a colonoscopy and the website for PHCS stated that Emily Carey at 4360 Fulton Dr NW Suite B is on the approved list but when I went there they stated that she works in Mentor Ohio, not Canton, Ohio.  Mentor is over an hour away but I filled out my paperwork at this office to get the colonoscopy completed at this office.  I told them that I want their best cash price.  My appt is 10/30/25.  The only other doctor near me to complete a colonoscopy on the website list was Sanjiv Khullar at 2727 Fulton Dr NW  Canton, OH and they said he does not do work with  PHCS anymore.
Please review and update the doctor list and advise if this is ok. 

Sent the following response:
Thanks for reaching out and letting us know about this. While we don’t have direct control over the Multiplan/PHCS website, I can absolutely reach out and make sure they are aware of the discrepancy.
 As for your upcoming colonoscopy on 10/30, if this is a preventive screening and you’re using a provider listed as in-network through PHCS, you should not need to request a cash price or pay anything out of pocket. Instead, present your benefit card at the appointment and ask the provider to submit the claim directly to Altrisk (info on card).
 If they seem unsure about the billing process, feel free to let us know. We can jump on a call with the provider to make sure everything is billed correctly.

AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-06-03 07:20:14', '2025-06-03 07:20:14'),
