  ('zcrm_1579374000165855008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162579002', 'Peter Wolf', NULL, '5/29/25
Peter called to check on the status of his mail order. I asked if he had downloaded the Health Wallet app and followed the instructions provided with the mail order. It was later confirmed that he had not downloaded the app and had mistakenly had his provider send the order to a previous company.
Peter mentioned that a previous representative had not assisted him properly, but I clarified that my colleague had, in fact, sent all the necessary information to help him complete the process. Upon further discussion, it became clear that Peter had not opened any of the emails my colleague sent and did not follow the instructions provided.
I then walked him through detailed, step-by-step instructions on how to navigate the Health Wallet app and place his order correctly. Since he mentioned that he was running low on medication, I advised him to consider picking it up in person to avoid a gap in treatment. However, he declined and stated that he preferred to receive it by mail.
I informed him that, based on standard processing times, it could take anywhere from 10 to 14 days for the mail order to arrive.

Ac', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-05-29 16:31:58', '2025-05-29 16:31:58'),
