  ('zcrm_1579374000165741091', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001538301', 'Brenda Smith', NULL, '5-28-25 Brenda is considering cancelling altogether. So, I left her a vm and let her know there are no penalties and I have other options that might be affordable for her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 17:00:24', '2025-05-28 17:00:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165741086', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000024844090', 'Valerie Yaw', NULL, '5-28-25 I spoke with Fletcher and he wants to review his options. He says no pre-x, so he can move to Premium Care or HSA. He aleady did his colonoscopy and he does wellness check bi-annually. I suggested the $1000 IUA for either but gave him the 3 middle prices for $1000, $1500 and $2500. He will decide by June 18th to be safe.  He''ll review them all. He''s working a full time job and this came quickly, so he wants time to think it over.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 16:50:08', '2025-05-28 16:50:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165741068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000140549002', 'Patricia Nilsen', NULL, '5-28-25 Patty needs ACA compliant ins for twins for college at Pepperdyne.  She upgraded her membership to add MEC and will only show MEC info for school. If that fails then she''ll have to pay for the college''s insurance which she doesn''t want to do. Premium HSA $1000 is $676 up from $558 for Premium Care. This will be effective for July 1st, in time to let college know the member ID, etc.  She knows there''s overlap with HAB and MEC. I let her know she can''t cancel the boys without cancelling her own HAB membership which she doesn''t want to do. So, she''ll keep everything intact.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 15:58:21', '2025-05-28 15:59:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165741063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060442195', 'Kristin Smith', NULL, '5-28-25 Kristin will re-enroll in Oct for a Nov. 1st start date when her employer benefits run out.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 15:31:45', '2025-05-28 15:31:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000165741049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165772002', 'Harper Phillips', NULL, '5-28-25 Must choose Secure HSA for compliance in VT!  He''s enrolling now for July 1st start date. He knows when to present insurance card and when not to.  He''s using cc since gets 2% cash back and is willing to give up the 1%.  Secure HSA $1000/$419 and $125/$25. All set and printing Quick Ref Guide and scheduling Welcome Call. He''ll cancel his current ins sometime in June.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 15:03:35', '2025-05-28 15:29:56'),
