  ('zcrm_1579374000165741038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '5-28-25 Elizabeth was bummed to lose Redirect since uses 12 chiro, urgent care and primary care. However she is deciding to change from $500 IUA to $1000 IUA to lower costs even more. She was paying $534.34 and then $599.46 for 2 months and then moved to Premium Care at $421.27. I told her to change to ACH which she''s doing now and also to $1000 IUA. So, now it will be $299/$1000 meaning she''ll save $300 a month to make up for the lost chiro, PCP and some wellness. She can easily pay for that out of the $300 per month = $3600 year. She also admitted that Redirect was a big challenge to work with but she had finally figured out how to use their app and get things paid for most of the time. Her son Reid is still working with the Debt Dismissal team to get his bills removed. The billing company recently changed hands, so he has to jump through more hoops again.  She''s also considering leaving Summit County because it''s so transient, her HOA fees are doubling and some others are tripling! She''s getting tired of the chaos and wants to find a nice community to live in, perhaps in another state. She''s thinking about OR and was shocked to hear WA has banned all MCS. She''ll avoid that state.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-28 14:27:20', '2025-05-28 14:49:47'),
