  ('zcrm_1579374000165458184', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011905055', 'Devorah Pearson', NULL, '5-23-25 Dev and Jeff (turning 50 July 11th) are very interested in Premium HSA or Premium Care. Dev is a teacher and their plan went up 17% this year and they can''t afford it. It''s $1300+ with UHC. Jeff has arthritis and Dev has auto-immune stuff that she''s been managing for 15-20 years already. They do annual wellness such as mammo and colonoscopy. Dev already did both this year and I told her about the 6 month wait for Premium Care or PHCS network for Premium HSA. Leaning towards Premium Care since the high cost items are shared up to the dollar amounts and childhood vax included.  If they choose Premium HSA it looks like UC Health Yampa Valley shows PHCS/Multi-Plan in network. So, they should be fine with either choices. Her benefits end around Aug. She may just opt out upon their annual renewal.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-23 12:58:42', '2025-05-23 12:58:42'),
