  ('zcrm_1579374000165338169', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165338131', 'Hannah Blatter', NULL, '5-21-25 Hannah is working for a company who just ended their health insurance 4-30-35. She thinks the company might be "tanking."  They said they''d cover them for one more month but there''s been no sign of that. She''s earning about $67,300 but that may not last. She did not qualify for a subsidy. She has something close to ulcerative colitis. She goes to Gastroenterology of the Rockies and sees Dr. David Gatof, Katie Vieira PA and Lisabeth Hall MD. They all showed up in the Cigna network. She takes mesalamine 1.2 delayed release 90 days supply.  She wanted to have co-pays for stuff. Chose Cigna Connect Flex 0 for June 1st start date. I had her upload her letter stating end of benefits on 4-30-25. She made the initial payment and knows to wait 7-10 days to set up ongoing payments. All set for now!   I showed her how to updated her income as well if/when necessary. She might qualify for a subsidy if she lands on unemployment.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-21 15:10:07', '2025-05-21 15:11:18'),
