  ('zcrm_1579374000164468013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082414002', 'Trinity Bieker', NULL, 'Trinity had questions regarding Pelvic exam. She gets Pelvic exams instead of pap smears since she had hysterectomy. She was wondering if it she can use her MEC card for it. LEt her know I would double check and we scheduled a follow up for tomorrow. She also wanted an update on the appeal for her Borland Groover visit. - LM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-05-06 17:44:01', '2025-05-06 17:44:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164468008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044571065', 'Anna Menz', NULL, 'Anna is experiencing hip pains. Did some tests and some more follow ups regarding this pain. Has paid $700 towards her IUA but has no opened a need yet. We called Sedera together to open the need, but they were not available, so she left a VM. She disconnected from there, but I called her back to see if there was anything else I could help with. - LM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-05-06 17:33:47', '2025-05-06 17:33:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164437158', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096331001', 'Darrell Porter', NULL, '5-6-25 Darrell called back and let me know Finray Solar has 23 Statutory W2 / Contractor employees. Finray Pays FICA and Payroll taxes and gives them a W2 at the end of the year but they are really still contractors and work their own hours. They have only 2 W2 employees and 6 1099 employees. They are no where close to 50. So, we will proceed as is.  Finray will offer MPB to their team and payroll deduct the membership amount from their pay for the contractors.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-06 16:17:31', '2025-05-06 16:17:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164437153', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027674121', 'WAHEED AYUBI', NULL, '5-6-25 Waheed is considering Covered CA but I explained it needs to be based off 2025 not 2024 income. Wife will be earning about $10K more this year. His kids qualified for Medicaid but he''s not confident in that bc someone changed some numbers and then dropped them and added them back. He''s going to run some numbers and ponder his best path. He knows I''ll be gone next week but he can cancel upon my return if he chooses. He''s also worried Zion could be pushed out of CA since the lawsuit shows nothing that differentiates the reason Sedera got pushed out vs Zion. It just stating they aren''t health insurance and acting like it and not in place prior to 1999. He''ll keep me posted on his decision.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-05-06 15:45:51', '2025-05-06 15:45:51'),
