  ('zcrm_1579374000164216190', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010543087', 'Tania Dibbs', NULL, '4/30/25
Tania inquired about coverage for a Pap smear, mentioning that she is currently going through menopause and has been unable to find a specialist in her area. Based on the nature of her concern, I wanted to ensure she received the most accurate information, as certain symptoms could lead a provider to classify the visit as diagnostic.
I respectfully asked if she was experiencing any specific symptoms that might influence coverage. At this point, Tania became noticeably frustrated and stated that all women experience symptoms during menopause. I apologized for any frustration caused and explained that my intention was to ensure she was informed, as diagnostic visits may not be covered under the ARM plan.
I encouraged her to speak with the provider’s office to confirm how the visit would be coded and reminded her that preventive Pap smears are typically covered under ARM, provided they are billed as preventive. AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-04-30 17:27:05', '2025-04-30 17:27:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164216185', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601108', 'Kevin Fechtmeyer', NULL, '4/30/25
sara called wanting to know what is covered with her plan, we went over detail how ARM is only intended to be used for preventative services under the ACA and guided her to the healthcare.gov to she could see the list for her self. I also explained how this is what makes her plans hsa eligble. We then went over some scenarios of when she would use Zion AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-04-30 17:18:51', '2025-04-30 17:18:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164216166', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000079033002', 'Lakshmi Murthy', NULL, '4/30/25
Lakishmi wanted to know how her plan works, I explained when she would use her mec and when to use the HS. I informed her that AM would pay 100% any preventative appointment and to just have the provider submit bills to po box. I expressed the importance of differentiating what is preventative and what is diagnostic in order to avoid confusion. Also assisted her with navigate the Multiplan website AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-04-30 17:14:08', '2025-04-30 17:14:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164216161', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011659218', 'Julie Harriman', NULL, '4/30/25
Julie wanted to update her mailing address sent her the form via email AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-04-30 17:10:30', '2025-04-30 17:10:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164216140', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069192234', 'Nathan Love', NULL, '4/30/25
Nathan wanted to know how to get his heart check out, I clarified to him that going to see a cardiologist would be considered specialty and would not be covered by the mec. I explained that this expense would be out of pocket and if something did arise he could potential open a sharing request. For the time being he opted to just have his regular wellness check AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-04-30 17:07:18', '2025-04-30 17:07:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164225119', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000164049002', 'Brett Humphreys', NULL, '4-29-25 Jeanette is 50 and Brett is 50. They live in Santa Rosa, CA. Jeanette watched the video and part of the interview. No tobacco. Brett has bi-polar but manages it very well on his own and no meds for years now. Jeanette had heart palpitations 3-4 years ago, in 2022 she thinks. She''s had nothing in the past 24 months. She''s been stuck with Kaiser which she says has been disastrous and paying $1400 per month. She has menopause that she''s managing now and knows that''s considered pre-x. But, understands she''ll pay for the meds and dr. visits related to that. For her and Brett they are choosing Secure HSA $1000/$733 for June 1st start date. She''s more traditional with her wellness care. So, they don''t really need HAB since they have to choose Secure HSA for compliance in CA. All set! 
4-30-25 Also, Brett is the one who is self-employed. So, we had him as the primary. He was going to enter his EIN but that field had disappeared. It''s fixed now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-04-30 16:57:52', '2025-04-30 17:00:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164225114', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165305002', 'Liv Ladendorff', NULL, '4-30-25 Liv is 49 and living in Longmont, CO now. She just started with a new travel company as NP. She can get ins with them but it''s $500-$600 a month. She decided to enroll in HAB but realized today that it won''t be worth the cost since she''s already done her wellness exams for the year and she''d only benefit for dental and gym. So, I requested a cancellation before her plan starts so she can get the $107 stopped. She has a foot problem that she needs a cortisone shot for and a dr. visit and possible an ultrasound. All of that will cost $700+. With the company group ins offered she can get those for $25 co-pay. She may use trad ins for now and then cancel when she knows she''s in the clear with her foot. She''s also going to try to use a massage therapist this week to see if that helps. If so, then she''s all set but still doesn''t really need HAB either way. She can join Premium Care any time moving forward.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-04-30 16:49:41', '2025-04-30 16:49:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000164225094', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010954107', 'Shelby (Hank) Carter', NULL, '4-30-25 Hank is interested in CARE+ and HAB for possibly him, wife and baby. His wife is losing her job and benefits soon. Hank is now 37, wife is 32. He was reminded of me by Ian McClendan! He''s currently on a BC/BS Nebraska Network Blue plan. I asked him how he''s on a NE plan and he doesn''t really know. He grew up in NE but hasn''t lived there  in years. He was on a Cigna plan prior to that and MPB before. He''s paying $1200 now for him and baby, so guessing to add his wife it would be $1800!  With HAB and CARE+ at $1000 IUA it will be $672+$250= $922 for the best plan and half the money!  He likely going to join HAB today for some combo of family members and then join Care+ for June 1st. He''s going to find out when his wife''s benefits end and will add her accordingly.  He would use the mental health, wellness checks, dental cleaning, gym membership, etc. So, it''s definitely worthwhile for him to join HAB and baby well checks without a network will be great for them.  For EC it will be $462/$1000 + $200 = $661. Plus the $125 Admin-Set up fee and make sure Ian gets the $100 Referral Fee.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-04-30 15:28:20', '2025-04-30 15:30:01'),
