  ('zcrm_1579374000164096032', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082414002', 'Trinity Bieker', NULL, '4/28/25
Trinity has been diagnosed with lynch syndrome and after doing some research i informed her the following 
If you''ve been diagnosed with Lynch syndrome, your colonoscopies are typically coded as diagnostic rather than preventive under most insurance policies, even though they are done for cancer prevention.

Preventive screenings are usually for asymptomatic individuals at average risk and done at standard intervals (e.g., every 10 years starting at age 45).
With Lynch syndrome, you''re considered high-risk, and colonoscopies are recommended more frequently (e.g., every 1–2 years starting at a younger age). Because of your diagnosis, insurance typically sees these as surveillance or diagnostic procedures, not routine preventive care

I told her to be on the safe side to please consult with her provider and ask how he would code it in order to guide her in the right direction AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-04-28 16:24:09', '2025-04-28 16:24:09'),
